1
00:01:51,415 --> 00:01:53,415


2
00:01:53,439 --> 00:01:54,505
Silverland...

3
00:01:55,563 --> 00:01:56,700
Silver as in the metal.

4
00:01:57,499 --> 00:02:01,420
Silverland means the Land of Silver.

5
00:02:03,260 --> 00:02:04,619
True to its name,

6
00:02:05,256 --> 00:02:07,166
silver was once endlessly mined here.

7
00:02:17,875 --> 00:02:18,359
But,

8
00:02:19,403 --> 00:02:21,600
because of it, ugly conflicts arose.

9
00:02:23,314 --> 00:02:27,920
The king used brute force, even starting a war to hoard all the silver.

10
00:02:28,940 --> 00:02:34,526
The realm fell into chaos and the people suffered, until a hero rose up in outrage.

11
00:02:35,420 --> 00:02:41,180
The hero took all the silver, built a silver ship, and sank it in a swamp.

12
00:02:42,864 --> 00:02:46,080
That secret is recorded here.

13
00:02:58,740 --> 00:02:59,925
Time passed,

14
00:03:00,563 --> 00:03:04,113
and the old legend was eventually forgotten.

15
00:03:12,923 --> 00:03:14,489
So that's how it is...

16
00:03:16,098 --> 00:03:18,912
Standing there reading for days on end... Geez.

17
00:03:19,176 --> 00:03:22,159
So, is there anything good in those?

18
00:03:24,909 --> 00:03:26,569
Who hit me on the head?!

19
00:03:27,133 --> 00:03:30,186
It's so damn long, I genuinely mistook it for something else!

20
00:03:30,256 --> 00:03:32,256
What was that for?!

21
00:03:36,956 --> 00:03:38,349
Serves you right!

22
00:03:39,329 --> 00:03:41,049
Old man! It's the master's report!

23
00:03:47,989 --> 00:03:49,456
Take this!

24
00:03:53,423 --> 00:03:55,423
Take that, you fool!

25
00:04:05,634 --> 00:04:07,999
Hey, let's take a quick break.

26
00:04:11,704 --> 00:04:14,773
A break won't hurt, right?

27
00:04:17,120 --> 00:04:18,120
What's this?

28
00:04:19,525 --> 00:04:23,426
Beneath three half-moons, a silver marsh slumbers in peace.

29
00:04:23,605 --> 00:04:25,973
As ripples spread, the silver ship rises,

30
00:04:25,997 --> 00:04:28,460
and the Silver Knight cries out to the moon:

31
00:04:28,560 --> 00:04:31,680
<i>O Moon, O Moon, aid me and grant me power!</i>

32
00:04:32,680 --> 00:04:36,120
This must be a clue showing the location of the silver ship!

33
00:04:37,160 --> 00:04:37,520
What?

34
00:04:38,020 --> 00:04:39,440
The legendary silver ship?

35
00:04:40,055 --> 00:04:42,993
You mean that silver ship nobody can find?

36
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:44,380
That's right.

37
00:04:44,695 --> 00:04:48,473
This text must point to where the silver ship is hidden.

38
00:04:51,600 --> 00:04:53,993
So where exactly is that place?

39
00:04:54,560 --> 00:04:55,806
Well...

40
00:04:57,765 --> 00:05:00,539
I don't understand it at all, but...

41
00:05:01,524 --> 00:05:05,540
Whatever it takes, use those clues to find that silver ship!

42
00:05:10,540 --> 00:05:11,780
...And that's how it went.

43
00:05:12,185 --> 00:05:15,826
Hmm. Is the silver ship really that great of a treasure?

44
00:05:16,430 --> 00:05:17,430
It really is.

45
00:05:17,620 --> 00:05:20,440
If it falls into the wrong hands, we'll be in big trouble.

46
00:05:21,060 --> 00:05:24,060
I'm a little worried since Duralumin knows about this, too.

47
00:05:26,060 --> 00:05:26,833
Sapphire!

48
00:05:27,060 --> 00:05:28,339
I have a great idea!

49
00:05:29,610 --> 00:05:30,853
A great idea?

50
00:05:31,855 --> 00:05:34,213
Listen, it's a really good one.

51
00:05:34,599 --> 00:05:37,453
Sapphire, you and I will find the treasure

52
00:05:37,477 --> 00:05:39,720
and share it with everyone in the kingdom!

53
00:05:41,166 --> 00:05:42,120
That's great!

54
00:05:42,280 --> 00:05:45,320
If we share it, everyone in the country will be rich, and

55
00:05:45,344 --> 00:05:47,480
Duralumin won't be able to use it for evil!

56
00:05:47,855 --> 00:05:49,160
That really is a great idea!

57
00:05:50,900 --> 00:05:52,126
Treasure hunt time!

58
00:05:52,300 --> 00:05:54,000
Search for the silver ship!

59
00:05:55,640 --> 00:06:02,020
Ah, crescent moon, crescent moon... silver ship, silver ship... ah, crescent moon...

60
00:06:02,865 --> 00:06:04,906
Did you figure something out, Your Grace?

61
00:06:05,545 --> 00:06:07,680
Ah, I want to get my hands on it no matter what.

62
00:06:08,005 --> 00:06:11,006
Man, it really is an amazing treasure, Nylon.

63
00:06:12,073 --> 00:06:12,580
What do you mean?

64
00:06:12,610 --> 00:06:14,593
Of course we want to get our hands on it!

65
00:06:15,360 --> 00:06:19,240
We'll get that amazing treasure, sell it off abroad, and hire an army.

66
00:06:19,490 --> 00:06:21,300
An insanely powerful army!

67
00:06:22,006 --> 00:06:23,333
And then...

68
00:06:29,470 --> 00:06:31,300
Got a bite!

69
00:06:31,913 --> 00:06:33,066
I caught one! I caught one!

70
00:06:33,853 --> 00:06:34,586
Oh my...

71
00:06:34,610 --> 00:06:37,571
Sakana-san, have you seen a ship made of silver

72
00:06:37,596 --> 00:06:38,826
at the bottom of this pond?

73
00:06:39,055 --> 00:06:41,120
A huge silver ship.

74
00:06:42,100 --> 00:06:44,320
You don't know? Ah, thank you anyway.

75
00:06:44,480 --> 00:06:46,280
Don't go getting caught again!

76
00:06:46,580 --> 00:06:48,540
You let my dinner get away!

77
00:06:51,470 --> 00:06:52,470
Hey, Mizutori-san.

78
00:06:52,705 --> 00:06:55,966
Is there a silver ship sunken in this water?

79
00:07:02,425 --> 00:07:04,780
Three half-moons... Three half-moons.

80
00:07:04,920 --> 00:07:07,040
A silver ship, a silver spring...

81
00:07:08,519 --> 00:07:11,379
Three half-moons...

82
00:07:11,750 --> 00:07:14,300
Don't be ridiculous! I mean moons!

83
00:07:14,895 --> 00:07:16,500
How could there be three of them?!

84
00:07:20,185 --> 00:07:21,540
Have you solved the riddle?

85
00:07:22,060 --> 00:07:25,760
Curse that Nylon! I told him to solve the riddle, what is he doing?!

86
00:07:27,421 --> 00:07:28,101
All right!

87
00:07:28,125 --> 00:07:29,660
Oh, Great Duke Duralumin!

88
00:07:29,795 --> 00:07:31,046
What do you mean, "All right"?!

89
00:07:31,125 --> 00:07:33,813
Don't tell me you were playing around instead of solving the riddle?

90
00:07:35,120 --> 00:07:37,940
Great Duke Duralumin, you must be joking.

91
00:07:38,590 --> 00:07:40,200
What about the riddle of the silver ship?

92
00:07:40,201 --> 00:07:41,420
Well, I'm almost there.

93
00:07:42,595 --> 00:07:45,040
What do you mean, "almost", Nylon?

94
00:07:46,160 --> 00:07:48,793
Well, as for the half-moons...

95
00:07:52,545 --> 00:07:53,405
This is it!

96
00:07:53,430 --> 00:07:54,430
I've got it!

97
00:07:56,570 --> 00:07:57,800
The half-moons mean archery bows!

98
00:07:58,085 --> 00:08:00,460
Three bows lined up—that means three half-moons!

99
00:08:00,815 --> 00:08:02,013
Look at that target over there!

100
00:08:02,895 --> 00:08:05,271
Those three half-moons must refer to Bow Mountain

101
00:08:05,296 --> 00:08:07,080
deep in the Northern Forest.

102
00:08:08,280 --> 00:08:10,773
That's where the silver ship is sunken!

103
00:08:17,840 --> 00:08:18,660
Three bows.

104
00:08:18,815 --> 00:08:20,540
It really is three half-moons.

105
00:08:27,700 --> 00:08:28,380
No way!

106
00:08:28,480 --> 00:08:29,220
There's no swamp!

107
00:08:29,300 --> 00:08:29,820
Damn it!

108
00:08:29,875 --> 00:08:31,440
So much for the Silver Swamp!

109
00:08:31,460 --> 00:08:32,460
Damn it!

110
00:08:44,965 --> 00:08:45,965
Water!

111
00:08:51,769 --> 00:08:53,680
Why was the grass moving?

112
00:08:54,275 --> 00:08:55,275
No, wait.

113
00:08:55,719 --> 00:08:58,260
Maybe this area used to be a swamp.

114
00:09:01,079 --> 00:09:02,079
I knew it!

115
00:09:02,300 --> 00:09:03,680
There used to be water here.

116
00:09:04,040 --> 00:09:07,313
Then what on earth was I riding all this time...?

117
00:09:20,715 --> 00:09:21,715
It's silver!

118
00:09:21,760 --> 00:09:22,180
It's silver!

119
00:09:22,340 --> 00:09:22,680
It's silver!

120
00:09:22,720 --> 00:09:23,140
It's silver!

121
00:09:23,300 --> 00:09:24,300
It's silver!

122
00:09:25,780 --> 00:09:26,320
It's silver!

123
00:09:26,440 --> 00:09:27,440
It's silver!

124
00:09:27,465 --> 00:09:29,280
Found you!

125
00:09:31,849 --> 00:09:32,849
I finally found you!

126
00:09:32,890 --> 00:09:34,860
There's a silver ship right under here!

127
00:09:38,065 --> 00:09:40,220
This has to be part of it!

128
00:09:44,220 --> 00:09:44,620
That's it!

129
00:09:45,186 --> 00:09:46,673
This is...the mast!

130
00:09:52,473 --> 00:09:54,326
That's it! Greenery!

131
00:09:58,985 --> 00:10:01,353
I found the silver ship!

132
00:10:36,829 --> 00:10:39,000
Moon, answer me.

133
00:10:39,509 --> 00:10:41,880
How many years have I slept?

134
00:10:42,080 --> 00:10:44,160
Who awakened me?

135
00:10:44,525 --> 00:10:46,780
Moon, tell me.

136
00:10:47,140 --> 00:10:49,540
Is calamity approaching again?

137
00:10:49,880 --> 00:10:53,120
Then grant me power!

138
00:11:06,589 --> 00:11:08,100
Hey, old Fukuro-san!

139
00:11:08,500 --> 00:11:11,885
It's a very old story, but have you ever heard of a silver ship

140
00:11:11,910 --> 00:11:14,626
sunk in a pond around here?

141
00:11:17,020 --> 00:11:17,873
I see.

142
00:11:17,980 --> 00:11:18,980
Thank you very much.

143
00:11:26,580 --> 00:11:28,340
Goodbye, Tink.

144
00:11:29,259 --> 00:11:30,840
Don't be discouraged, Sapphire.

145
00:11:31,300 --> 00:11:33,000
Let's look again tomorrow.

146
00:11:33,790 --> 00:11:35,030
- Goodbye!
- Goodbye!

147
00:11:44,429 --> 00:11:45,720
Three half-moons in a row!

148
00:11:50,270 --> 00:11:51,560
That's Bow Mountain!

149
00:11:51,710 --> 00:11:53,040
Opal, stop!

150
00:11:55,750 --> 00:11:57,815
So that's what the three half-moons meant!

151
00:11:58,499 --> 00:11:59,386
Hurry, Opal!

152
00:11:59,460 --> 00:12:00,460
It's Bow Mountain!

153
00:12:22,009 --> 00:12:24,580
No matter how much we search, there's no swamp.

154
00:12:24,729 --> 00:12:29,040
According to the text, the Silver Swamp should be around here, though.

155
00:12:30,120 --> 00:12:31,120
What's that?

156
00:12:35,329 --> 00:12:36,540
Who are you?

157
00:12:37,200 --> 00:12:38,306
Why are you here?

158
00:12:39,205 --> 00:12:41,280
I am Prince Sapphire of this land.

159
00:12:41,845 --> 00:12:43,566
I came looking for the legendary swamp.

160
00:12:43,985 --> 00:12:46,360
So it was you who woke me.

161
00:12:46,700 --> 00:12:47,860
You greedy prince!

162
00:12:48,145 --> 00:12:50,386
I won't let you get a single step closer to the Silver Swamp!

163
00:12:51,779 --> 00:12:53,900
So the Silver Swamp really is here!

164
00:12:54,555 --> 00:12:56,693
Curse you, greedy human!

165
00:13:04,885 --> 00:13:06,200
What are you doing?

166
00:13:29,886 --> 00:13:31,800
Oh no!

167
00:13:35,813 --> 00:13:40,740
O Moon, O moon, help me!

168
00:13:41,209 --> 00:13:44,880
Will you give me strength.

169
00:13:45,080 --> 00:13:46,080
Now!

170
00:13:50,859 --> 00:13:52,420
O Moon!

171
00:13:53,760 --> 00:13:55,200
What on earth happened?

172
00:13:59,513 --> 00:14:00,360
It vanished!

173
00:14:00,385 --> 00:14:01,385
No way!

174
00:14:24,535 --> 00:14:25,720
Vampire bats!

175
00:14:28,060 --> 00:14:30,066
I have to escape before this fire goes out...

176
00:14:41,705 --> 00:14:42,705
A door!

177
00:14:43,439 --> 00:14:44,680
It's hot!

178
00:14:51,080 --> 00:14:51,813
Damn it!

179
00:14:52,045 --> 00:14:53,045
It's getting closer!

180
00:14:54,065 --> 00:14:55,640
We have to get inside!

181
00:15:10,646 --> 00:15:11,646
I made it!

182
00:15:42,806 --> 00:15:43,660
Hurry!

183
00:15:43,685 --> 00:15:44,740
Move it!

184
00:15:45,029 --> 00:15:47,306
Dawdle any longer and dawn will break!

185
00:15:47,820 --> 00:15:50,106
Come on, hurry to Bow Mountain!

186
00:15:51,220 --> 00:15:51,880
Nylon!

187
00:15:51,915 --> 00:15:53,900
Did it really weigh 100 tons?

188
00:15:54,270 --> 00:15:57,004
Absolutely. Judging by that mast, 100 tons is an understatement.

189
00:15:57,029 --> 00:15:58,860
 It's enough to break this crane.

190
00:15:59,360 --> 00:16:00,240
I see!

191
00:16:02,260 --> 00:16:03,260
Incredible!

192
00:16:03,295 --> 00:16:04,320
Look how huge it is!

193
00:16:04,630 --> 00:16:06,120
Even the shells are made of silver!

194
00:16:06,539 --> 00:16:09,115
With this much, we could share it with everyone in the world!

195
00:16:09,140 --> 00:16:10,240
Do not touch the ship!

196
00:16:10,390 --> 00:16:11,580
That voice... It's him!

197
00:16:11,969 --> 00:16:13,160
I will not hand over this ship!

198
00:16:13,380 --> 00:16:16,320
The foolish blood of that greedy king flows in your veins!

199
00:16:16,530 --> 00:16:17,806
Who on earth are you?!

200
00:16:18,800 --> 00:16:22,740
I am the Silver Spirit, guardian of this ship for centuries!

201
00:16:30,209 --> 00:16:32,400
The mountain of treasure is just ahead, sir!

202
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:33,286
Hurry!

203
00:16:33,480 --> 00:16:34,480
We're close!

204
00:16:37,598 --> 00:16:38,525
Please listen to me!

205
00:16:38,735 --> 00:16:42,800
I want to share this with everyone in the kingdom... no, the whole world!

206
00:16:42,801 --> 00:16:43,801
Silence!

207
00:16:43,860 --> 00:16:45,785
Your foolish ancestor said the same thing,

208
00:16:45,809 --> 00:16:48,660
trying to keep all the silver for himself!

209
00:16:49,493 --> 00:16:50,177
Because of that,

210
00:16:50,201 --> 00:16:52,437
peaceful Silverland was thrown into turmoil—

211
00:16:52,461 --> 00:16:55,344
war broke out, burning thousands of homes and

212
00:16:55,368 --> 00:16:57,780
claiming thousands of lives!

213
00:16:59,560 --> 00:17:01,626
I won't be fooled by your words!

214
00:17:02,060 --> 00:17:03,320
I'm not tricking you!

215
00:17:03,525 --> 00:17:05,460
I don't want silver, gold, or jewels!

216
00:17:05,794 --> 00:17:07,800
I just want to share it with the poor!

217
00:17:08,125 --> 00:17:09,125
Please believe me!

218
00:17:09,159 --> 00:17:10,359
I'll do anything for that!

219
00:17:12,240 --> 00:17:13,240
Shut up!

220
00:17:18,249 --> 00:17:19,653
Hear me, Silver Sprite!

221
00:17:20,029 --> 00:17:22,119
I don't want silver, gold, or jewels!

222
00:17:22,435 --> 00:17:24,619
I just want to give them to the poor!

223
00:17:26,500 --> 00:17:27,166
Silver Sprite!

224
00:17:27,460 --> 00:17:28,460
Are you listening?

225
00:17:29,800 --> 00:17:31,100
Silver Sprite!

226
00:17:31,780 --> 00:17:33,026
Silver Sprite!

227
00:17:33,420 --> 00:17:34,986
Silver Sprite!

228
00:17:36,489 --> 00:17:37,880
Where did you go?

229
00:17:52,078 --> 00:17:53,411
Your body...

230
00:17:53,435 --> 00:17:57,930
Only my soul, which refuses to let silver disrupt the peace,

231
00:17:57,955 --> 00:17:59,940
has possessed this armor!

232
00:18:08,600 --> 00:18:09,600
Look out!

233
00:18:15,569 --> 00:18:17,280
Did you save me?

234
00:18:17,340 --> 00:18:17,880
Why?

235
00:18:18,010 --> 00:18:19,010
Why?

236
00:18:51,720 --> 00:18:52,400
Silver Sprite!

237
00:18:52,686 --> 00:18:53,299
Silver Sprite!

238
00:18:53,505 --> 00:18:54,222
Prince...

239
00:18:55,039 --> 00:18:56,226
You've awakened?

240
00:18:56,345 --> 00:18:57,100
I have a favor to ask!

241
00:18:57,300 --> 00:18:58,300
Look at that!

242
00:18:58,540 --> 00:18:59,349
That's...

243
00:18:59,373 --> 00:19:00,321
Yes!

244
00:19:00,394 --> 00:19:04,660
Fools consumed by greed have come to claim this silver ship!

245
00:19:10,840 --> 00:19:11,940
Lower the crane!

246
00:19:12,819 --> 00:19:13,945
Lower the crane!

247
00:19:19,969 --> 00:19:22,800
I can't move without bathing in moonlight!

248
00:19:23,364 --> 00:19:26,980
Wear this armor in my place and protect the silver ship!

249
00:19:27,380 --> 00:19:29,980
This armor will surely protect you!

250
00:19:30,993 --> 00:19:31,706
Understood.

251
00:19:36,359 --> 00:19:38,780
A fish... No, we hooked the ship!

252
00:19:39,119 --> 00:19:41,299
That's it! Raise the crane!

253
00:19:41,719 --> 00:19:42,719
Raise the crane!

254
00:19:51,509 --> 00:19:52,853
Raise it faster!

255
00:20:01,580 --> 00:20:02,315
Here it comes!

256
00:20:02,340 --> 00:20:03,400
It's coming up!

257
00:20:15,040 --> 00:20:16,266
It's the silver ship!

258
00:20:16,699 --> 00:20:17,780
Come on, don't dawdle!

259
00:20:17,880 --> 00:20:19,113
Pull it up quickly!

260
00:20:26,125 --> 00:20:27,125
What is that?

261
00:20:27,549 --> 00:20:30,340
So you are the fools blinded by greed!

262
00:20:31,449 --> 00:20:34,200
Who on earth... are you?!

263
00:20:34,849 --> 00:20:36,780
I am the Silver Spirit, guardian of this swamp!

264
00:20:37,064 --> 00:20:39,620
I won't let greedy fools have this ship!

265
00:20:39,640 --> 00:20:40,273
Bows!

266
00:20:40,339 --> 00:20:41,799
Shoot that monster with your bows!

267
00:20:44,729 --> 00:20:45,915
It's useless!

268
00:20:58,999 --> 00:20:59,693
It's no use!

269
00:20:59,749 --> 00:21:01,680
Spears are no match for my bow!

270
00:21:01,824 --> 00:21:03,653
It's a monster!

271
00:21:03,750 --> 00:21:04,960
Wait!

272
00:21:13,089 --> 00:21:15,580
I had no idea a monster like that existed!

273
00:21:15,660 --> 00:21:17,200
Hide behind that furnace!

274
00:21:17,834 --> 00:21:19,180
Nylon, take a look!

275
00:21:19,920 --> 00:21:20,920
It's coming!

276
00:21:21,599 --> 00:21:22,800
Well, Nylon?

277
00:21:22,879 --> 00:21:24,227
Right now, it's fighting the soldiers...

278
00:21:24,251 --> 00:21:25,481
 I've got it!

279
